WEBVTT

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:39.410
Stop!

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:45.770
Rikiishi Toru prepared for this day by enduring a dreadful weight loss, going down two weight classes.{timing- 3 liner - split}

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:50.280
And Yabuki Joe, from the unknown Tange Gym, stands against him.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.990
This match is being heralded as the greatest eight-round match in history,

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:58.630
and considering their grudge, this is surely a showdown of destiny!

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.330
What's wrong? You don't look so happy.

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:02.550
You're ahead in points, Joe!

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:05.430
Yeah, you're doing good. Rikiishi's losing his balance.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:06.690
Just keep this up!

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.560
I'm in a bad spot this match.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:11.700
You're in a bad spot? That ain't true!

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.860
Rikiishi's losing his posture from missing all those uppercuts,

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.060
while your straights are hitting him!

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:19.270
You just need to keep this up! No need to worry!

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:23.460
I may be hitting him, but my punches barely reach him after I dodge his uppercuts.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:27.710
Those punches hit him, but nothing more. They couldn't kill a fly.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.590
And it's Rikiishi I'm facing.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:34.730
This is no ordinary match.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:37.840
I'd have to win with something more than just a few measly points.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:42.470
Punches that can hit, but can't even kill a fly... You're exactly right.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:48.320
But on the other hand, Rikiishi's mighty uppercuts will seal his win if one hits you.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.850
Yeah, I'd say the odds are stacked against you.

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:55.400
But if Joe rushes him head-on, he'll be more likely to be hit by an uppercut!

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:58.360
I know that! Just shut up!

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:08.230
Oh, well. No point in struggling against it now.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:19.720
I'm sure my wild instincts will figure something out

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:21.740
while we're exchanging blows.

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:23.360
I just have to wait for that.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:43.530
Go for it! Go for it, Bro Joe!

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:47.530
Pummel his face in!

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.060
Rikiishi! Knock him straight to the moon!

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.480
Get him!

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:19.210
What the hell's your problem, Rikiishi?

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:22.700
Why are you so fixated on those big swings?

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:24.900
What's your problem, Rikiishi?

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.170
I expected more of you!

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:29.200
Don't you know that won't work against Yabuki?

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:45.380
What are you, a fan? You keep blowing wind in my face!

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.560
Hang on.

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:11.650
I've always given Rikiishi his due,

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.370
but this isn't the sane Rikiishi.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.650
The only ones here are me{limpakos- suggestion: split after 'me' and join the rest with the next line}

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:22.520
and the half-crazy Rikiishi who's suffered through weight loss and become a demon of willpower.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:27.760
Maybe he can't think of anything to do but uppercuts.

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:31.680
And his stamina can't be what it used to be, not after that weight loss.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:36.750
If that's the case... If that's the case...

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:39.330
Then Rikiishi may not even be worth fearing!

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:45.610
I guess...

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:47.610
I'll risk taking an uppercut or two,

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.650
so I can get five or six hits in and end the match!

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.810
Hey, what's the matter?

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:04.280
We didn't pay to see a staring contest!

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:11.100
Do it, Bro Joe! Do it now!

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:19.590
Come on, go! What's the matter with you two?

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:26.860
Here he comes!

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:30.070
That uppercut's not gonna-

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:36.740
You moron! That almost hit you!

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:39.870
Don't just stand there! One slip could get you killed!

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:49.550
I... I know! It's a good thing I felt an abnormal bloodlust from him,

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.180
and swayed back in the nick of time!

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.280
I shouldn't underestimate him.

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:58.640
He has fearsome punches that he's trained for a long time!

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:02.930
Look! That uppercut just barely scratched Joe's cheek, and...

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:12.650
What a terrifying, razor-sharp uppercut.

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:13.680
Look, Nishi!

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.420
That's the bell! Go back to your corner!

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:22.740
Hey, Joe!

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.480
Nishi! Get ready to stop the bleeding!

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:33.900
In the second round, Rikiishi's razor-sharp punch has slashed Joe's cheek!

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:38.820
Yabuki's managed to escape Rikiishi's punches with his desperate Sway Backs this round...

00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:43.480
That was a close call. But you got in a shot in the second half.

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:44.900
Keep it up!

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:48.590
Okay, enough of your half-assed comforting!

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:55.180
I know where I stand better than anyone.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:09:00.810
I've never felt this shameful, this wretched in my whole life!

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:04.520
Rikiishi's not gonna budge, no matter how many punches I get in!

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:09.580
But look at what his punches do when they just graze me!

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:13.030
Rikiishi's amazing! I now know the depths of his power!

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:15.920
I've had enough of your constant whining!

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:17.890
That's not like you at all!

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:24.540
Okay, Joe. It looks like we have no choice.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:28.790
It's a little dangerous, but why don't you attack a little more assertively?

00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:31.550
Is... Is there a way?

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:35.310
He needs a lot of space to throw an uppercut.

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:40.010
So you gotta get right into his swinging space and hook him from the right and left!

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:43.760
Got it, Joe? Get in there as soon as he misses!

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:44.520
All right?

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:47.580
The timing's the problem, old man.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:53.320
Don't you worry. You're agile enough to slip past his uppercut.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:56.320
I see. Short hooks, huh...

00:09:56.320 --> 00:10:02.030
It's a little plain for me, but that's the only way I can attack at this point.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:07.000
Yeah. They may be short hooks, but you punch strong enough!

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:12.450
You should have enough power to send the tottering Rikiishi to the mat!

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.710
You gotta do this, Joe!

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:20.810
This'll be your greatest obstacle!

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:33.320
All right, I'll try, old man. Thanks.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:52.450
Hey, wh-what did Joe just say?

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:55.460
I think he said "thanks"...

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:06.860
"Thanks"?

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:11.290
He's never thanked me before!

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:16.430
There's something different about that guy today.

00:11:16.430 --> 00:11:17.570
Something must've changed in him!

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.160
Joe! Now!

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:29.450
Gotcha!

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:46.350
Go for it, Joe!

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:54.730
Now's your chance! Go for it, Joe! Joe!

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.950
Go! Give it to him!

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:13.460
Rikiishi-kun!

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:17.460
What power! Yabuki got those punches in brilliantly!

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:21.970
He's suddenly switched from a Sway Back, points-based strategy to a damage-based one!

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:33.550
Don't rest, Joe! Don't give Rikiishi any space!

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:34.440
Stick to him!

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:39.810
I got it! No need to shout so loud! You'll raise your blood pressure.

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:42.690
What's wrong, Rikiishi?
 No more uppercuts? Bring it! C'mon!

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:08.870
Joe, hit me to your heart's content, while you still have the chance.

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:12.700
Eventually, you won't be able to do a thing!

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:40.340
Hit me to your heart's content, while you have the chance.

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:43.710
Eventually, you won't be able to do a thing!

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:48.250
What the hell are you mumbling for?

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:53.910
I hate the way you're smiling with a bloody nose!

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:55.180
I really hate false courage!

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:57.890
False courage, you say?

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:04.360
You're free to interpret my smile however you choose...

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:08.610
This isn't good!

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:14.240
Rikiishi knows he can't swing uppercuts in close quarters, so he's switched to short hooks himself!

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:18.810
Way to go, Rikiishi!

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:20.130
Go get 'im!

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:31.840
This has become an intense exchange of blows!

00:14:31.840 --> 00:14:34.520
Blood's flying off Rikiishi, and sweat's flying off Yabuki!

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:37.390
This has become a match worthy of being called the match of the century!

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:49.360
Joe! You don't need to fear Rikiishi's short hooks!

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:51.810
Just keep fighting in close quarters!

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:54.620
You can match him in an exchange of short hooks!

00:14:57.900 --> 00:15:02.610
At the very least, you have a better chance here than dodging those uppercuts!

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:03.920
Go! Go!

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:12.670
That was close!

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:17.020
He feinted and went back into his uppercut strategy!

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:22.980
Dammit...

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:28.190
Son of a...

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:31.680
Don't go head-on, idiot! Stop!

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:34.850
It's too risky to charge in now!

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:37.330
Stick to him! Bring it in to a close quarters fight!

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:39.330
Shut up!

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:44.080
Stop yelling all the time! You're ruining my focus! Just shut up!

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:06.390
I... I can't get close to him.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:09.940
I feel like his uppercuts are getting sharper.

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:12.880
Or is it my movements getting dull?

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:17.410
Let's keep going.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:21.370
Come on, come on!

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:24.250
What's the matter?

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:26.570
Now!

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.250
He's down! Yabuki's down!

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:38.540
And what an amazing counter from Rikiishi!

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:44.550
Get to a neutral corner!

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:02.040
Gonna try it again?

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:09.830
Joe!

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:13.630
And Yabuki's down! He's down again!

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:21.010
Damn you...

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:25.770
Out of my way!

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:28.370
Don't get up, Joe, you idiot!

00:17:28.370 --> 00:17:30.270
Stay down till the count of eight!

00:17:32.560 --> 00:17:34.780
Stop! Stop!

00:17:32.560 --> 00:17:33.650
<i>Dammit...</i>

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:39.280
You moron! Why didn't you listen to me?

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:43.790
If you tried pulling that again, you'd have three downs this round, and you'd lose!

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:46.750
Nishi! Stop the blood again!

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:48.840
What's wrong with you, Yabuki?

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:50.750
Can't keep your balance?

00:17:53.350 --> 00:17:55.840
I can't do that anymore, old man.

00:17:55.840 --> 00:18:00.180
Every time I charge in at him, he hits me with a counter.

00:18:01.030 --> 00:18:04.090
I hate to admit it, but he's right.

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:06.450
I'm starting to run out of options.

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:09.650
Rikiishi's a fearsome one.

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:17.650
It turns out his total uppercut strategy

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:21.660
wasn't just to keep you from doing the Cross Counter.

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:24.940
He's ended up keeping you from throwing any strong punches!

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:26.640
Got it, Joe?

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:32.590
Yabuki has gone down twice in the third round!

00:18:32.990 --> 00:18:38.380
Ishida-san, it seems that all the life has gone from Yabuki's corner, wouldn't you say?

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:43.840
I don't blame them. It'd be impossible to get back up

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:47.250
after even the strategy you trained so hard for had been outclassed.

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:02.990
But in contrast, Rikiishi's corner is giving off an air of confidence!

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:05.260
He's already tied his prey up.

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:09.540
Now all that's left is to figure out how to cook it.

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:10.040
What was that?

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:13.000
Don't just spew shit like that!

00:19:13.350 --> 00:19:14.460
I'll kill you!

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:18.900
No, Joe! Cut it out!

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:17.280
<i>Piece of shit!</i>

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:20.550
I'm completely pissed off now!

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:25.670
Listen, Joe! Struggling won't get you anywhere!

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:29.400
Your only choice is to get in there and hit him, whatever the cost!

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:30.310
You got me?

00:19:34.510 --> 00:19:36.890
But how the hell am I supposed to get in there?

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:39.450
If I get in, he'll hit me with a short hook,

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:42.530
but if I keep my distance, he'll attack me with those uppercuts!

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:43.530
I can't do a thing!

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:51.910
No matter how I struggle, I'm shut in on all sides!

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:56.300
I've never dreaded the bell like this in my entire life!

00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:08.010
Get him, Rikiishi!

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:16.900
What's wrong, Joe? Aren't you gonna get in close?

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:25.410
If you're not coming at me, you leave me no choice but to go to you!

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:31.610
Stay in there, Joe!

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:34.290
Don't be afraid to get in close!

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:48.200
It's all or nothing...

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:51.810
I'm in!

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:05.330
Yeah, that's the way! Hit him, Joe! Pincer him!

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:25.960
I guess I didn't teach you that short hooks are meaningless yet.

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:27.710
If that's what you'll do...

00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:01.290
He did it!

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:03.590
He's done it! He's done it!

00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:05.760
Two minutes and forty seconds into the fourth round!

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:08.020
Rikiishi's signature uppercut has connected!

00:22:08.020 --> 00:22:08.840
Yabuki's down!

00:22:09.380 --> 00:22:13.780
That intense strike hit Yabuki square in the jaw!

00:22:14.150 --> 00:22:15.060
What do you think, Ishida-san?

00:22:16.650 --> 00:22:17.890
I'd say that about does it!

00:22:17.890 --> 00:22:23.070
Has this put an end to the fated showdown between Rikiishi and Yabuki?

00:22:23.500 --> 00:22:25.070
Can Yabuki get back up?

00:22:25.840 --> 00:22:27.070
Get up!

00:22:27.070 --> 00:22:29.070
G-Get up, Joe!

00:22:56.220 --> 00:23:02.070
The grand battle between the men who risk death is now entering the second half.

00:23:02.490 --> 00:23:06.760
But Rikiishi's furious attacks continue as normal.

00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:09.850
Rikiishi's punches fly, right then left, left then right.

00:23:10.650 --> 00:23:14.840
And before Rikiishi's cold, calculated, terrifying power,

00:23:15.510 --> 00:23:18.830
Joe's strategies are crushed one by one.

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:21.550
Joe's arms and legs are torn off completely,

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:23.080
and it seems as though he'll submit!

00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:28.450
But just then, Joe plans to escape his predicament!

00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:33.150
Joe's mighty punch hits Rikiishi while he's tired,

00:23:33.150 --> 00:23:34.790
and Rikiishi's finally down!

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:39.230
The audience swallows their spit as the match unfolds.

00:23:40.700 --> 00:23:43.600
But as Rikiishi barely manages to stand up again,

00:23:44.060 --> 00:23:49.610
he uses his trump card, Joe's trademarked No Guard strategy!

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:53.640
Joe is struck dumbfounded before Rikiishi's scheme!

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:58.660
Now, as they literally battle it out to the end,{tlc- do they actually say "literally"}

00:23:58.660 --> 00:24:02.030
and as Joe and Rikiishi use up their last ounces of strength,

00:24:02.030 --> 00:24:03.650
which way is tomorrow!?

00:24:18.070 --> 00:24:21.110
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:18.070 --> 00:24:21.110
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:24.950
Oira boxer

00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:24.950
I am a boxer.

00:24:25.740 --> 00:24:32.710
Yuuhi ga giragira otoko no yume wa

00:24:25.740 --> 00:24:32.710
The evening sun glitters upon the dreams of men!

00:24:34.420 --> 00:24:38.380
Minna wa kono ore wo nasakemuyo to iu

00:24:34.420 --> 00:24:38.380
Everyone says that I am merciless.

00:24:38.380 --> 00:24:40.420
Tsuki ni hoete hitori

00:24:38.380 --> 00:24:40.420
Howling at the moon alone.

00:24:42.510 --> 00:24:46.640
Oyanashi yadonashi no na mo nai boxer wa

00:24:42.510 --> 00:24:46.640
A parentless, homeless, nameless boxer

00:24:46.640 --> 00:24:49.640
Kusari wo kamikitta Yeah Yeah!

00:24:46.640 --> 00:24:49.640
has bitten off his chains! Yeah, yeah!

00:24:51.350 --> 00:24:54.270
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:51.350 --> 00:24:54.270
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:55.480 --> 00:24:57.980
Oira boxer

00:24:55.480 --> 00:24:57.980
I am a boxer.

00:24:59.110 --> 00:25:06.240
Asahi ga noboru yo otoko no mune ni {removed the Woo, but otherwise japanese is unchanged - Reed}

00:24:59.110 --> 00:25:06.240
The morning sun rises upon the hearts of men!
